WEBVTT

00:11:29.678 --> 00:11:31.271
That doesn't help them choose.

00:11:31.295 --> 00:11:34.561
They ask, "So, where do I look
for authority? Where is wisdom found?"

00:11:34.585 --> 00:11:37.767
And we say, "Look inside yourself.
Find your passion. You do you."

00:11:37.791 --> 00:11:40.445
But the "you" is exactly
the thing that hasn't formed.

00:11:40.469 --> 00:11:43.169
And so, basically, they're looking
for a way to find out

00:11:43.193 --> 00:11:44.822
what to devote their lives to,

00:11:44.846 --> 00:11:47.733
and we have nothing to say
except, "You do you."

00:11:47.757 --> 00:11:50.748
No wonder life in the 20s
right now is a very hard life,

00:11:50.772 --> 00:11:54.545
because there's no shared sense of,
"This is what is most worth wanting."

00:11:55.475 --> 00:11:58.586
CA: I mean, it is quite hard to picture
what the advice should be.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:02.313
I don't think we want to go back to
"The Graduate" and, "One word: plastics."